"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nOne of the things I had wanted to try since planning the Australia trip was a Public BBQ.  \nFree communal BBQ facilities are set up throughout the parks for anyone to use.\n\nWe came prepared with foil trays, scissors, and tongs.  \nIf you don't have them, you can buy them at a nearby supermarket.\n\nWe first headed to a nearby large supermarket to buy ingredients and water for the BBQ.  \nThere were many types of meat, so we carefully picked what seemed like a good amount at a reasonable price.  \n\nWe initially debated between lamb and beef, but the lamb portions were either too much or too little, so we settled on beef.  \nThere were many cuts of beef to choose from, so we selected carefully.\n\nWe also picked up button mushrooms to have as a garnish with the beef.  \nThey were enormous.  \nWe bought salt too, but ended up not using it.\n\nWhen we arrived at the Public BBQ area, no one else was there, so we had the whole thing to ourselves.  \nPress the button on the grill to start it up, and once the indicator turns green, it's ready to use.\n\nWe placed the beef, the butter that came with it, and the mushrooms onto the foil tray and started grilling.  \nThe heat turned out to be weaker than expected, and the foil tray was too thick, so the meat ended up steaming rather than grilling.\n\nWe had also brought along instant noodles bought cheap in Melbourne and tried heating water for them on the grill,  \nbut the temperature barely rose enough to produce steam, let alone bring it to a boil.  \nWe had no choice but to make do with steamed beef and lukewarm water for dinner.\n\nEven so, the meat itself was good quality, and it was surprisingly tender and delicious.  \nThe mushrooms grilled alongside were especially tasty — cooked with butter, they were genuinely delicious.  \nIf you're planning to grill here, mushrooms are a must-bring.\n\nThe instant noodles hadn't softened since there was no boiling water,  \nso we improvised by pouring them into a foil tray and heating them on the grill again.  \nIn the end, the noodles were a failure due to the water temperature issue, but we ate every last bite because we were craving something spicy.\n\nThere was a bathroom nearby, so we could quickly rinse off the scissors and tongs we used.\n\nIf you plan to grill meat, using thin foil trays or laying down cooking foil directly will work much better than thick foil trays.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"